WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.718
I wanted something which would give

00:00:02.718 --> 00:00:05.162
me a broader toolkit that I could

00:00:05.162 --> 00:00:07.528
use at this stage of my career.

00:00:07.528 --> 00:00:09.333
I also wanted to have access

00:00:09.333 --> 00:00:11.687
to a global international cohort of

00:00:11.687 --> 00:00:13.413
people who were doing lots

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:14.904
of interesting things

00:00:14.904 --> 00:00:16.399
in their own careers.

00:00:16.399 --> 00:00:18.417
A program which combine the two,

00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:19.641
which I could do from

00:00:19.641 --> 00:00:20.730
my dining table.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:24.847
[MUSIC]

00:00:24.847 --> 00:00:26.239
I realized there was something

00:00:26.239 --> 00:00:27.690
different about this program.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.451
The program pushed me outside my

00:00:30.451 --> 00:00:31.780
comfort zone in

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:34.036
many of the assignments.

00:00:34.036 --> 00:00:36.270
It forced me to look at myself

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:37.856
in different ways.

00:00:37.856 --> 00:00:40.326
In my job, I have directly applied

00:00:40.326 --> 00:00:41.353
course work.

00:00:41.353 --> 00:00:43.476
Things like business model design,

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:45.187
designing organizations for

00:00:45.187 --> 00:00:47.241
creativity and innovation in terms

00:00:47.241 --> 00:00:48.541
of how I run meetings,

00:00:48.541 --> 00:00:49.576
how I run my team.

00:00:49.576 --> 00:00:51.316
Before I started LEAD,

00:00:51.316 --> 00:00:53.752
I definitely thought of myself as

00:00:53.752 --> 00:00:56.188
a finance professional in a bulge

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:58.458
bracket firm in New York City.

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:00.434
Now I think of myself as

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:03.450
an intrapreneur within my company

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.570
trying to build projects systems.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:08.457
Managing people in different

00:01:08.457 --> 00:01:10.872
countries, with different cultural

00:01:10.872 --> 00:01:13.135
backgrounds, and yet trying to get

00:01:13.135 --> 00:01:15.406
them to work towards the same goal.

00:01:15.406 --> 00:01:17.701
Return on investment in LEAD is

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:19.996
a lot more than just the classes

00:01:19.996 --> 00:01:21.595
you're attending.

00:01:21.595 --> 00:01:23.601
It is about applying them and

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:26.110
then seeing how others are applying

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:26.617
them.

00:01:26.617 --> 00:01:28.742
LEAD has really taught me that

00:01:28.742 --> 00:01:30.187
you can be impactful

00:01:30.187 --> 00:01:31.632
in anything you do.

00:01:31.632 --> 00:01:34.453
It's an investment in myself as I

00:01:34.453 --> 00:01:36.971
design the next phase of my own

00:01:36.971 --> 00:01:37.590
life.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:43.425
[MUSIC]

